Events and live transcripts fan out to every Radulf web process via a polling events tailer and a per-run transcript watcher registry (spec 25 decision 5).
- `src/server/eventsTail.ts`: every process (all roles, started from `src/server/boot.ts`) polls the `events` table every `RADULF_EVENTS_TAIL_INTERVAL_MS` ms (default 500) for ids past the last seen and re-emits them on the local bus, skipping locally-emitted ids (`wasEmittedLocally` in `src/server/events.ts`); it writes nothing, so the table stays the only durable copy.
- `src/server/transcriptWatchers.ts`: the web role keeps exactly one `startTranscriptPush` watcher per running run per process, started on `run.started`/`iteration.started` or by a `RADULF_TRANSCRIPT_SCAN_INTERVAL_MS` (default 5000) scan of `runs`, following a loop run's latest iteration file, and stopped on `run.finished` or when the row stops running. `src/server/stage.ts` no longer starts a push; `src/server/scoping.ts` still does (stays in the web process); the SSE route and browser are unchanged; no client-interest protocol.
- `make check-split` (`src/server/splitProcesses.test.ts`, gated by `RADULF_SPLIT_CHECK=1`) boots two web-only and one worker-only process and asserts events and live transcripts fan out across processes.
